y=100 width=290 height=420; frame cream #f5e9d2 outer, inner panes; mullions. Outside sky pale warm blue #b9cdd0 with hills maybe. Morning sunlight comes from left. Window partially open? Could add curtain on right. Light beams as polygons with low opacity from window toward lower right, across table and floor.\n\nMaybe background left window and right side a shelf / hanging utensils? But requirement small table. Don't overcomplicate. Add simple framed art? Maybe no people but kitchen context: chair? The table front view could have chair behind? Not required. Keep table alone. Maybe a small vase? No, exact items only likely avoid extra. Add retro tile backsplash? Maybe table against wall; window left. Floor.\n\nTable: wooden, warm muted amber #b68157 with top #c68f5d, side edge #9d6e49, apron, legs. Seen from front: top elliptical? \"seen from front\" means table with front face and top slightly visible. Flat illustration, we can draw top as rounded rectangle with a slight ellipse top surface. Top at y 630, x 415 to 945. Table height to y 810. Legs x 465/860. Table top thickness. Maybe small round table? \"small kitchen table, seen from the front.\" Could be rectangular. Composition.\n\nObjects:\n- Three red apples. Use apple shape: two overlapping circles/squircle paths with top dimple, stem, leaf maybe green. Exactly three. Could place 2 near left center and 1 slightly behind? Need all clearly red. Maybe a row at left of table: apples at (500, 600), (560, 610), (530, 565). But newspaper needs room. Let's map tabletop usable x 440-930 y 540-635.\n- Blue mug at x ~780, y~570, mug body 70x85, handle right or left; word MONDAY in white/cream capitals. Should sit on tabletop. Add steam? Morning coffee maybe no steam; optional no.\n- Folded newspaper with cat asleep on top. Newspaper at right? Table maybe wide, objects could be: apples left, mug center-left? Newspaper right with cat. Cat must be on top of folded newspaper. We can make newspaper a folded stack on right side x 650-930 y 565-620, cat curled on top. Need cat sleeping, gray. Newspaper visible below with lines and header. Cat perhaps curled oval with head. Ensure cat on top. Blue mug maybe center left 720? Let's sketch.\n\nTable top x=380 to 980 y=610. Tabletop top ellipse-ish horizontal rect. Place apples on left: x 460, 515, 565 y around 580. Mug at x 650 y 545 base 620. Newspaper folded on right: x 740-960 y 585-630, cat on top around 760-930 y 520-590. Cat may obscure newspaper but still visible edges with \"The Morning Post\" maybe.\n\nBut mug could clash. Maybe table x 350-1000, objects:\n- three apples on left 430-580.\n- blue mug at 650-740.\n- newspaper folded with cat at 780-980.\nWidth good.\n\nTable top y=630 with objects resting around y=630 baseline. Table top surface can be visible at y=600? Let's establish:\nbackground floor starts y=760. Table top slab top surface at y=610, front edge thickness 28 to y=642. Table legs down to 830. Objects sit baseline at y=630? Actually top surface visible from y 610 to 638? We draw table top as rounded rectangle x=360 y=610 w=660 h=44, with top highlight. Objects baseline at 628. Table top could be viewed slightly from above, but from front means objects stand up from surface around y=615. Hmm.\n\nBetter: tabletop as a horizontal ellipse (perspective subtle) at y=620 height 38, plus front edge rounded rect. Objects baseline 608 in the ellipse center? But front view, tabletop top surface not fully visible. Flat design can use simple horizontal bar. Let's do table top rounded rect from x 350 y 600 to 1010 y 644, fill wood. Objects baseline at y=606? If they rest \"on\" the top, usually bottom at top surface line y=600. Add shadows beneath at y=602. Table top bar extends y=600-642. Objects bottom at 600? Then they sit on back edge line. In front view, table top surface line is y=600. Yes objects stand on it and hide the back part of top. The tabletop's rear edge at y=600. That's fine.\n\nTable front legs down from x 410 and 900 y 642 to 835; crossbar y 760. Table height 235. Top width 660. Looks small-ish.\n\nMaybe chair not. Window left above table.\n\nCat: curled sleeping on newspaper. Gray body curled oval, darker gray stripes, head tucked; eyes closed. Tail curled. Need recognizable. Cat on top of folded newspaper: newspaper stack at right maybe 720-960, folded with visible pages, sheets slightly offset, text lines. Cat's body on top y 510-595. Cat body uses rounded shape and head at left with ears, closed eyes, pink nose, whiskers. Gray #8b8d87 with muted darker #71736f and light #a8aaa3. Sleep \"z\" marks? optional, maybe 3 z's. Could add to convey asleep. Flat.\n\nSunlight: window left x 70-360 y 80-470. Light beams diagonally from window across room to right/down. Use polygons with #fff3c9 opacity .35. The light falls across table and objects. Since flat vector, maybe hard-edged beams with transparent warm overlay. Add subtle window shadow on wall? Add sun beams from window corners: \n- polygon from (90,160) to (355,110) to (950,780) to (470,900) with opacity. Could overlay across table but not obscure. Better 2 beams with 0.10-0.15 opacity.\n- sunlight patches on table/floor as ellipse/polygon.\nNeed avoid making messy. Perhaps a large polygon from window toward bottom center-right in pale yellow at 0.16; add another narrower band.\n\nWindow itself: frame dark wood #80634f; outside soft warm pale blue. Maybe curtains warm cream on each side. Morning sky. Add a small plant? No.\n\nWarm muted palette:\nwall #ead9c2\nwall lower panel? There is wainscoting maybe #d6bfa6 with chair rail y=560? Hmm window extends to 470. Back wall warm beige. Floor #b99b7b. Rugs? no.\nWood table #a96f4c, highlights #bd855b, dark #865538.\nApples #b8463c red with darker #96372f, highlight #cd6254, stems brown, leaf sage.\nMug #496b83 blue, dark #3b566c, band? Word \"MONDAY\" in #f7ead2. Handle. Maybe small white speckles? Keep.\nNewspaper #d8cfbd off-white, lines #a89e8c, headline maybe \"DAILY\".